Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:56:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] TORQUEBYPASS9050: HT9050 skips the index-check torque read
 for now -- EastSun 1008 WAR0361 ('Index Z1 torque not read in 5 s, E-044') ->
 'bypass it; the torque read is not verified yet'.

atester_FinePitch.cpp FP case 12110 (910 :2415): on HT9050 with g_W906Ht9050TorqueReadBypass (end of file, default true) no torque read / compare -- InitWriteAndCheckMotorTorqueTask and straight to 12200, so the torque limit is still written back to 300 %. Turn the global off (or drop the line) once the read is verified. Other machines: 910. Same line + end of file.
tests/test_fp9050_index.cpp: fidelity edit list + :2415; new [F6] check 'bypass on -> 12200, no WAR0361'; the F6 / F8 torque-read checks run with the bypass off. FP9050_Pure, FP9050_Index, E044TorqueWait passed. Debug and release linked. WORKLOG row 197.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 atester_FinePitch.cpp       | 4 +++-
 docs/WORKLOG_MACHINE.md     | 1 +
 tests/test_fp9050_index.cpp | 8 ++++----
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

